  "memo": "White alder ranges from southern California to Washington, western Idaho, and western Nevada. In California, it occurs in much of the state but is less common along the immediate coast. It's an entirely riparian tree, never found far from permanent riverbanks or canyon streams. White alder has flat, egg-shaped leaves with small teeth along the leaf edges.",
